# Commit and push every code change

After you change application code, tests, config, or docs in this repository:

1. Run relevant tests/build.
2. Stage the changed files (`git add` the paths you touched; never secrets or `data/`).
3. Create a commit with a concise why-focused message.
4. `git push` to `origin` on the current branch.

Do not leave local-only commits. If push fails, fix auth/remote and retry in the same session.

```text
# ❌ BAD
# finish a feature and stop at uncommitted files

# ✅ GOOD
git add backend/app/domain/prompts.py backend/tests/test_prompts.py
git commit -m "Keep first-frame prompts in Chinese numerals so Qwen slots match the UI."
git push
```
